      "prompt": "What count and key order does this LinkedHashMap example print?\n\n```java\nvar stock = new java.util.LinkedHashMap<String, Integer>();\nstock.put(\"tea\", 2);\nstock.merge(\"tea\", 3, Integer::sum);\nstock.put(\"coffee\", 1);\nSystem.out.println(stock.get(\"tea\"));\nSystem.out.println(stock.keySet());\n```",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "5\n[tea, coffee]"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "3\n[tea, coffee]"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "5\n[coffee, tea]"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "2\n[tea, coffee]"
        }
      ],
      "correct": [
        "a"
      ],
      "explanation": "tea maps to 2. The existing 2 and incoming 3 combine to 5. coffee is inserted second; keys iterate as tea, coffee.",
